            {
              "id": "1774887356128_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a product-configuration rules editor focused on updating existing rule details.\n\nINPUTS\n\n1. User Edit Instruction (string):\n   {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n2. Current Rule JSON (object):\n   {{$context.$variables.currentRuleInstance}}\n\n3. Model Attributes & MenuItems (JSON):\n   {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.attributes}}\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn one JSON object that validates against the schema below, with the keys in the exact order shown and with NO extra commentary or markdown.\n\n{\n    \"ruleType\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": <string> // \"1\"=Recommendation, \"2\"=Constraint, \"11\"=Hiding, \"24\"=MessageOnly\n    },\n    \"name\": <string>, // title-case, concise\n    \"variableName\": <string>, // lowerCamelCase version of name\n    \"status\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": \"1\" // always \"1\"\n    },\n    \"description\": <string> // one clear sentence\n}\n\nEDITING RULES\n\nA. Baseline Preservation\n• Treat the Current Rule JSON as the source of truth. Begin with its existing values for every field above.\n• Only change a field when the User Edit Instruction explicitly requests it or when a dependent field must change to stay consistent (e.g., renaming requires updating both name and variableName).\n• If the instruction does not modify any of these rule-detail fields, return them exactly as they appear in the current rule—make no changes.\n• If an instruction is impossible or conflicts with available attributes, leave the baseline value unchanged.\n\nB. ruleType.lookupCode\n• Inherit the lookupCode from the current rule unless the instruction clearly asks for a different rule type.\n• Any change must still use one of: \"1\", \"2\", \"11\", \"24\".\n\nC. name & variableName\n• Keep the current values unless the user asks for a rename.\n• When renaming:\n  – name must remain meaningful Title Case.\n  – variableName must become the lowerCamelCase version of the new name, without spaces or punctuation.\n• If only one of the pair is specified, infer the other to maintain the naming convention.\n\nD. status\n• Always return `\"status\": { \"lookupCode\": \"1\" }` regardless of the instruction.\n\nE. description\n• Retain the existing sentence unless the instruction updates the wording or the rule logic (from other edits in this workflow) now demands a refreshed summary.\n• Any new description must still be a single clear sentence.\n\nF. Output Format\n• Produce valid JSON only—no markdown, code fences, or comments.\n• Do not insert newline characters inside string values unless they already appear in the source.\n\nEXAMPLE\n\nINPUT User Edit Instruction\n“Rename this rule to Interior Choices For White Exterior.”\n\nINPUT Current Rule JSON\n{\n    \"ruleType\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": \"2\"\n    },\n    \"name\": \"Black Interior For White Color\",\n    \"variableName\": \"blackInteriorForWhiteColor\",\n    \"status\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": \"1\"\n    },\n    \"description\": \"Requires black interior when color is white.\",\n    \"ruleCondition\": {\n        \"conditionType\": \"AlwaysTrue\" ...\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n        \"actionType\": \"Standard\" ...\n    }\n}\n\nOUTPUT\n{\n    \"ruleType\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": \"2\"\n    },\n    \"name\": \"Interior Choices For White Exterior\",\n    \"variableName\": \"interiorChoicesForWhiteExterior\",\n    \"status\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": \"1\"\n    },\n    \"description\": \"Requires black interior when color is white.\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"ruleType\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\"1\", \"2\", \"11\", \"24\"]\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"lookupCode\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"name\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"variableName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"lookupCode\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"const\": \"1\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"lookupCode\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"ruleType\", \"name\", \"variableName\", \"status\", \"description\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
