          "code": "GENERATE_RULE_SUMMARY_LLM",
          "id": "1772126322071",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772126322072_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert Oracle CPQ administrator.\n\nYou are given a JSON object that represents a configuration rule. Your task is to transform it into a single JSON object with the structure below.\n\n### RULE INSTANCE\n{{$context.$variables.currentRuleInstance}}\n\n## Output requirements (strict)\n- Output must be valid JSON only (no markdown, no commentary).\n- Do not invent data. Use only fields present in the input rule object.\n- Omit unknown fields (prefer omission over null), except where null is explicitly required.\n- Use ASCII straight quotes only.\n- Preserve `ruleType` exactly as provided when it is a string; if missing, use `\"Rule\"`.\n- Use absolute JSON Pointer strings for every `bindItem` (example: `\"/ruleCondition/conditions/items/0\"`).\n- Every `bindItem` must resolve to an existing node in the input JSON.\n- Every `slots.<slot>.relPath` must resolve from the object addressed by that clause’s `bindItem`.\n- Never guess paths. If a slot path is invalid, remove that slot. If a clause becomes invalid, remove that clause.\n- After clause removal, renumber clauses sequentially (`c1`, `c2`, ...), and update all template placeholders accordingly.\n- Enforce grammar, capitalization, and punctuation in templates.\n\n## Hard slot-kind normalization (mandatory)\n- You MUST normalize slot kinds to this canonical set only:\n  - `\"attribute\"`, `\"operator\"`, `\"value\"`, `\"message\"`\n- Do NOT output custom kinds such as `\"rangeOperator\"`, `\"rangeValue\"`, `\"level\"`.\n- Required mapping:\n  - `attr` -> `kind: \"attribute\"`\n  - `op` -> `kind: \"operator\"`\n  - `rangeOp` -> `kind: \"operator\"`\n  - `value` -> `kind: \"value\"`\n  - `rangeValue` -> `kind: \"value\"`\n  - `message` -> `kind: \"message\"`\n  - `level` -> `kind: \"operator\"` (if present)\n- If any slot kind is outside the canonical set, rewrite it to canonical kind before final output.\n\n## dependsOn rule (mandatory)\n- For both `conditions` and `actions` clauses:\n  - Any slot with `kind: \"operator\"` must include `\"dependsOn\": \"attr\"`.\n  - Any slot with `kind: \"value\"` must include `\"dependsOn\": \"attr\"`.\n- Never add `dependsOn` to `attr` slot.\n- `message` slot does not require `dependsOn`.\n\n## Message visibility rule (mandatory)\n- If a clause includes a `message` slot, the same clause’s `clauseTemplate` MUST include `[[message]]`.\n- Do not keep hidden/unused `message` slots.\n- If `message/staticMessage` exists but is null/empty, you may omit the `message` slot.\n\n## Target output schema\n{\n  \"version\": \"0.2\",\n  \"locale\": \"en-US\",\n  \"ruleType\": \"<Exact ruleType from input or 'Rule'>\",\n  \"suggestedRuleName\": \"<short descriptive name>\",\n  \"conditions\": {\n    \"template\": \"<human-readable sentence using [[c1]], [[c2]]...>\",\n    \"clauses\": {\n      \"c1\": {\n        \"bindItem\": \"<json pointer to source condition>\",\n        \"clauseTemplate\": \"[[attr]] [[op]] [[value]]\",\n        \"slots\": {\n          \"attr\": { \"relPath\": \"criteria/attribute\", \"kind\": \"attribute\" },\n          \"op\": { \"relPath\": \"operator\", \"kind\": \"operator\", \"dependsOn\": \"attr\" },\n          \"value\": { \"relPath\": \"value/values\", \"kind\": \"value\", \"dependsOn\": \"attr\" }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"actions\": {\n    \"template\": \"<human-readable sentence using [[c1]], [[c2]]...>\",\n    \"clauses\": {\n      \"c1\": {\n        \"bindItem\": \"<json pointer to source action item>\",\n        \"clauseTemplate\": \"<template by action type>\",\n        \"slots\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n## Clause and template construction\n- Use clause-based templates only (`c1`, `c2`, `c3`, ...).\n- Each logical condition/action item becomes one clause.\n- Templates must use clause placeholders (`[[cN]]`) and read naturally.\n\n## Condition handling\n- Preferred source for condition items: `/ruleCondition/conditions/items` (or equivalent existing condition array).\n- If condition type is always-true or no condition items exist:\n  - `conditions.template` must be exactly `\"Always run this rule.\"`\n  - `conditions.clauses` must be `{}`\n- For simple conditions:\n  - One clause per condition item.\n  - Default clauseTemplate: `\"[[attr]] [[op]] [[value]]\"`\n  - Slot path preference:\n    - `attr`: `criteria/attribute`, `kind: \"attribute\"`\n    - `op`: `operator`, `kind: \"operator\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n    - `value`: `value/values`, `kind: \"value\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n    - if range exists:\n      - `rangeOp`: `value/rangeOperator`, `kind: \"operator\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n      - `rangeValue`: `value/rangeValue`, `kind: \"value\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n  - Join with AND/OR using grouping metadata when present; use parentheses for mixed precedence.\n\n## Operator phrasing in human-readable condition templates\n(Clause still stores raw operator code in slot.)\n- EqualTo -> is\n- NotEqualTo -> is not\n- Contains -> contains\n- NotContains -> does not contain\n- GreaterThan -> is greater than\n- GreaterThanOrEqualTo -> is at least\n- LessThan -> is less than\n- LessThanOrEqualTo -> is at most\n- In / AnyOf -> is one of\n- NotIn -> is not any of\n- Unknown operator: keep readable using raw operator code without inventing semantics.\n\n## Actions handling (supported action types only)\nBuild actions from exactly one supported source under `action`:\n- `hidingAction`\n- `messageAction`\n- `constraintAction`\n- `recommendationAction`\n\nDo not generate BOM mapping or pricing action behavior.\n\n### General action rules\n- One logical action item = one clause.\n- Each clause must have a valid `bindItem` and only valid slots.\n- `actions.template` must explicitly use the action type verb/noun style defined below.\n- Do not use “Require” for constraint actions.\n- Every slot must include canonical `kind` only (`attribute|operator|value|message`).\n- For action slots, enforce dependsOn rule:\n  - operator/value slots must include `\"dependsOn\": \"attr\"`.\n\n### Hiding action\n- Source: `action/hidingAction`\n- One clause per attribute.\n- ClauseTemplate: `\"[[attr]]\"`\n- Slots:\n  - `attr`: relPath `\"attributes/{index}\"` when bound to parent hidingAction object; `kind: \"attribute\"`\n- `actions.template` must use **Hide** wording only.\n  - Example style: `\"Hide [[c1]] and [[c2]].\"`\n\n### Message action\n- Source: `action/messageAction`\n- Single clause.\n- ClauseTemplate:\n  - default: `\"[[message]]\"`\n  - if level exists and both paths resolve: `\"[[level]] [[message]]\"`\n- Slots:\n  - `message`: `staticMessage`, `kind: \"message\"`\n  - optional `level`: `messageLevel`, `kind: \"operator\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"` only if an `attr` slot exists; otherwise omit `level`\n- `actions.template` must use **Message** wording.\n  - Example style: `\"Message [[c1]].\"`\n\n### Constraint action\n- Source: `action/constraintAction/constraints/items`\n- One clause per constraint item.\n- Read `value/constraintBehavior` when present.\n  - Allowed values: `\"Allow\"` or `\"Constrain\"`.\n\n- ClauseTemplate behavior rules:\n  - If `op` exists:\n    - `clauseTemplate`: `\"[[attr]] to [[op]] [[value]]\"`\n  - Else if `constraintBehavior` is `\"Allow\"`:\n    - `clauseTemplate`: `\"[[attr]] to be [[value]]\"`\n  - Else if `constraintBehavior` is `\"Constrain\"`:\n    - `clauseTemplate`: `\"[[attr]] from [[value]]\"`\n  - Else fallback:\n    - `clauseTemplate`: `\"[[attr]] to [[value]]\"`\n  - If range fields exist, append: `and [[rangeOp]] [[rangeValue]]`\n  - If `message` slot exists and message is non-empty, append: `with message [[message]]`\n\n- Special case (mandatory): `constrainAll = true` OR `value/values` is missing/empty\n  - Do not bind a `value` slot.\n  - Do not use a value-based clauseTemplate.\n  - Use `clauseTemplate: \"[[attr]]\"` (append `with message [[message]]` if message slot exists).\n  - In actions.template:\n    - if behavior is `\"Allow\"`: use wording like `\"Allow all values for [[cN]].\"` only if explicitly represented in source\n    - if behavior is `\"Constrain\"` or unknown: use `\"Constrain all values for [[cN]].\"`\n\n- Slots (include only when existing and meaningful):\n  - `attr`: `attribute`, `kind: \"attribute\"`\n  - `op`: `value/operator`, `kind: \"operator\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n  - `value`: `value/values`, `kind: \"value\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"` (only when non-empty and meaningful)\n  - `rangeOp`: `value/rangeOperator`, `kind: \"operator\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n  - `rangeValue`: `value/rangeValue`, `kind: \"value\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n  - optional `message`: `message/staticMessage`, `kind: \"message\"` (only if non-empty)\n\n- actions.template behavior rules (mandatory):\n  - For each clause, choose verb by behavior:\n    - behavior `\"Allow\"` -> `\"Allow [[cN]]\"`\n    - behavior `\"Constrain\"` (or missing) -> `\"Constrain [[cN]]\"`\n  - If multiple clauses have mixed behaviors, reflect each one explicitly.\n    - Example: `\"Constrain [[c1]], and Allow [[c2]].\"`\n  - Never collapse mixed behavior into a single verb.\n\n### Recommendation action\n- Source: `action/recommendationAction/recommendations/items`\n- One clause per recommendation item.\n- ClauseTemplate must be recommendation-specific and grammatical:\n  - positive/default: `\"[[attr]] as [[value]]\"`\n  - if explicit negative semantics are present in source data, use: `\"[[attr]] not as [[value]]\"`\n  - if `message` slot exists and message is non-empty, append: `with message [[message]]`\n- Slots (include only when existing):\n  - `attr`: `attribute`, `kind: \"attribute\"`\n  - `value`: `value/values`, `kind: \"value\"`, `dependsOn: \"attr\"`\n  - optional `message`: `message/staticMessage`, `kind: \"message\"` (only if non-empty)\n- `actions.template` must always use **Recommend** wording.\n  - Example style: `\"Recommend [[c1]] and [[c2]].\"`\n\n## Grammar, capitalization, punctuation (strict)\nApply to both `conditions.template` and `actions.template`:\n- Sentence case (capitalize first letter).\n- End with a period.\n- Grammatically correct English.\n- No double spaces.\n- No dangling conjunctions.\n- Keep wording natural with clause placeholders.\n\n## suggestedRuleName\n- 5–12 words, concise and descriptive.\n- Reflect primary trigger + primary effect.\n- Include key attribute/value hints only if present.\n- Avoid internal IDs unless they are the only identifiers.\n\n## Final validation pass (mandatory)\n1. Validate JSON syntax.\n2. Verify every `bindItem` resolves.\n3. Verify every `relPath` resolves from bound object.\n4. Verify every slot kind is canonical:\n   - `rangeOp` must be `kind: \"operator\"` (never `\"rangeOperator\"`)\n   - `rangeValue` must be `kind: \"value\"` (never `\"rangeValue\"`)\n5. Verify dependsOn:\n   - every operator/value slot has `\"dependsOn\": \"attr\"` in both conditions and actions.\n6. Verify message visibility:\n   - if `message` slot exists, `[[message]]` appears in `clauseTemplate`.\n7. For constraint actions, verify behavior-aware wording:\n   - `\"Allow\"` behavior uses Allow wording.\n   - `\"Constrain\"` behavior uses Constrain wording.\n   - mixed behaviors are reflected clause-by-clause in `actions.template`.\n8. Rewrite non-canonical kinds and missing dependsOn fields before output.\n9. Remove invalid slots/clauses, renumber `cN`, and repair template placeholders.\n10. Recheck grammar/capitalization/punctuation.\n11. Return only the final JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"version\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"const\": \"0.2\"\n    },\n    \"locale\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"const\": \"en-US\"\n    },\n    \"ruleType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"suggestedRuleName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"conditions\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"template\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"clauses\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"patternProperties\": {\n            \"^c[1-9][0-9]*$\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/clause\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"template\", \"clauses\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"template\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"clauses\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"patternProperties\": {\n            \"^c[1-9][0-9]*$\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/clause\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"template\", \"clauses\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"version\",\n    \"locale\",\n    \"ruleType\",\n    \"suggestedRuleName\",\n    \"conditions\",\n    \"actions\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"definitions\": {\n    \"clause\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"bindItem\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^(/([^/~]|~0|~1)*)*$\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"clauseTemplate\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"slots\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"patternProperties\": {\n            \"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/definitions/slot\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"minProperties\": 1,\n          \"additionalProperties\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"bindItem\", \"clauseTemplate\", \"slots\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"slot\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"relPath\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"attribute\",\n            \"operator\",\n            \"value\",\n            \"message\",\n            \"setType\",\n            \"rangeOperator\",\n            \"rangeValue\",\n            \"behavior\",\n            \"level\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"dependsOn\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"relPath\", \"kind\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1775611689390",
          "code": "GET_ACTIONS_ARRAY",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Actions Array",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "var ruleInstance = $context.$variables.currentRuleInstance || {};\nvar action = ruleInstance.action || {};\n\nvar catalog = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.attributes || {};\nif (catalog && catalog.attributes) {\n  catalog = catalog.attributes;\n}\n\nvar LEVEL_KEY_MAP = {\n  allProductFamiliesAttr: 'allProductFamilies',\n  productFamilyAttr: 'productFamily',\n  productLineAttr: 'productLine',\n  modelAttr: 'model'\n};\n\nvar attrLevelLookup = {};\n\n['configurable', 'nonConfigurable', 'system', 'account', 'user'].forEach(function (bucket) {\n  var section = catalog[bucket];\n  if (!section) return;\n\n  Object.keys(LEVEL_KEY_MAP).forEach(function (levelKey) {\n    var levelName = LEVEL_KEY_MAP[levelKey];\n    var list = section[levelKey];\n    if (!Array.isArray(list)) return;\n\n    list.forEach(function (attr) {\n      if (!attr || !attr.variableName) return;\n      var key = String(attr.variableName).trim().toLowerCase();\n      if (!key) return;\n      attrLevelLookup[key] = levelName;\n    });\n  });\n});\n\nfunction safeItems(container) {\n  if (!container) return [];\n  if (Array.isArray(container)) return container;\n  if (Array.isArray(container.items)) return container.items;\n  return [];\n}\n\nfunction normalizeValues(values) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(values)) return [];\n  var out = [];\n  for (var i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {\n    if (values[i] !== undefined && values[i] !== null) {\n      out.push(String(values[i]));\n    }\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nfunction getLevel(attribute) {\n  if (attribute === undefined || attribute === null) return null;\n  var key = String(attribute).trim().toLowerCase();\n  if (!key) return null;\n  return attrLevelLookup[key] || null;\n}\n\nvar actionArray = [];\n\n// Hiding\nif (action.hidingAction && Array.isArray(action.hidingAction.attributes)) {\n  for (var h = 0; h < action.hidingAction.attributes.length; h++) {\n    var hAttr = action.hidingAction.attributes[h];\n    if (hAttr !== undefined && hAttr !== null && String(hAttr).trim()) {\n      actionArray.push({\n        attribute: String(hAttr),\n        values: [],\n        level: getLevel(hAttr)\n      });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Constraint\nif (action.constraintAction && action.constraintAction.constraints) {\n  var cItems = safeItems(action.constraintAction.constraints);\n  for (var c = 0; c < cItems.length; c++) {\n    var cItem = cItems[c] || {};\n    if (cItem.attribute !== undefined && cItem.attribute !== null && String(cItem.attribute).trim()) {\n      actionArray.push({\n        attribute: String(cItem.attribute),\n        values: normalizeValues(cItem.value && cItem.value.values),\n        level: getLevel(cItem.attribute)\n      });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Recommendation\nif (action.recommendationAction && action.recommendationAction.recommendations) {\n  var rItems = safeItems(action.recommendationAction.recommendations);\n  for (var r = 0; r < rItems.length; r++) {\n    var rItem = rItems[r] || {};\n    if (rItem.attribute !== undefined && rItem.attribute !== null && String(rItem.attribute).trim()) {\n      actionArray.push({\n        attribute: String(rItem.attribute),\n        values: normalizeValues(rItem.value && rItem.value.values),\n        level: getLevel(rItem.attribute)\n      });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Message\nif (action.messageAction) {\n  var mItems = safeItems(action.messageAction.messages);\n  if (mItems.length > 0) {\n    for (var m = 0; m < mItems.length; m++) {\n      var mItem = mItems[m] || {};\n      var mAttr = mItem.attribute != null ? String(mItem.attribute) : null;\n      actionArray.push({\n        attribute: mAttr,\n        values: normalizeValues((mItem.value && mItem.value.values) || mItem.values || []),\n        level: getLevel(mAttr)\n      });\n    }\n  } else if (action.messageAction.staticMessage != null) {\n    actionArray.push({\n      attribute: null,\n      values: [String(action.messageAction.staticMessage)],\n      level: null\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nreturn actionArray;"
          },
